### MITPass Phase 3 demo: event lifecycle, registrations, waitlist, idempotency, eligibility. All through the gateway.
### Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or IntelliJ's HTTP client, top to bottom, on fresh seed data.
### The expected status is in each request's title. Seeded accounts (password Passw0rd!):
###   organizer.a@mitpass.test (owns TECHFEST26, AIWS26, MINIQUIZ26), 2026509001@student.annauniv.edu (Priya, CSE, year 1),
###   2026505014@student.annauniv.edu (Arun, AERO, year 1)
### Domain events: RabbitMQ UI http://localhost:15672 (mitpass/mitpass) → Queues → mitpass.events.tap → Get messages.
### Portal: http://localhost:8090 shows the same flows in a browser.

@gw = http://localhost:8080

### --- log in ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# @name organizer
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "organizer.a@mitpass.test", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

###
# @name priya
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "2026509001@student.annauniv.edu", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

###
# @name arun
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "2026505014@student.annauniv.edu", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

### --- 1. Event lifecycle (state machine, D10) ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### 201 Organizer A creates a 1-seat event (starts DRAFT; allowedTransitions = [PUBLISHED]). Change the code on a rerun.
# @name created
POST {{gw}}/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "HTTPDEMO1", "title": "HTTP demo event", "categoryId": 1, "venueId": 1, "capacity": 1,
 "startsAt": "2099-11-14T03:30:00Z", "endsAt": "2099-11-14T09:30:00Z",
 "registrationOpensAt": "2099-10-01T03:30:00Z", "registrationClosesAt": "2099-11-13T12:30:00Z",
 "eligibleDepartments": [], "minYear": null, "maxYear": null}

### 409 illegal-transition: DRAFT can't go LIVE; allowedStates = ["PUBLISHED"]
POST {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}/transitions
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"to": "LIVE"}

### 200 DRAFT → PUBLISHED, with a reason for the history
POST {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}/transitions
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"to": "PUBLISHED", "reason": "Programme confirmed"}

### 200 PUBLISHED → REGISTRATION_OPEN (allowedTransitions: REGISTRATION_CLOSED, CANCELLED; never LIVE: only the scheduler starts events)
POST {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}/transitions
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"to": "REGISTRATION_OPEN"}

### 200 The audited history: creation, PUBLISHED, REGISTRATION_OPEN (who, when, why, MANUAL/SCHEDULER)
GET {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}

### --- 2. Register, waitlist, promotion ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 200 Priya checks first: eligible, seatsLeft 1
GET {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}/eligibility
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}

### 201 Priya registers: CONFIRMED (and a RegistrationConfirmed event goes to RabbitMQ)
# @name priyaReg
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": {{created.response.body.id}}}

### 201 Arun registers: the event is full → WAITLISTED, waitlistPosition 1
# @name arunReg
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{arun.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": {{created.response.body.id}}}

### 200 Priya cancels: promotedRegistrationId = Arun's registration (same transaction).
### The tap queue now shows registration.cancelled, registration.waitlist-promoted, registration.confirmed with this correlation id.
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations/{{priyaReg.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}
X-Correlation-Id: http-demo-promotion
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "Can't make it"}

### 200 Arun is CONFIRMED, viaPromotion true
GET {{gw}}/api/registrations/{{arunReg.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{arun.response.body.accessToken}}

### 409 illegal-transition: a cancelled registration can't be cancelled again (allowedStates [])
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations/{{priyaReg.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}

### 200 The organizer's view of the event's registrations
GET {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}

### 200 Priya's registrations, newest first (the cancelled one stays as history)
GET {{gw}}/api/registrations/me
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}

### --- 3. Idempotency-Key (D10) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 201 Priya registers again with a key (re-registering after a cancellation is allowed: a new registration)
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: http-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": {{created.response.body.id}}}

### 201 The same request again: the same body, header Idempotent-Replayed: true, nothing new created
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: http-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": {{created.response.body.id}}}

### 422 idempotency-key-mismatch: the same key for a different request
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}
Idempotency-Key: http-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": 1}

### 409 already-registered: without a key, a second registration is refused
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": {{created.response.body.id}}}

### --- 4. Eligibility ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 200 Find AIWS26 (open to CSE, IT, AIDS only)
# @name aiws
GET {{gw}}/api/events?q=Applied

### 200 Arun (AERO) is not eligible: reasons = ["Open to AIDS, CSE, IT only (you are in AERO)"]
GET {{gw}}/api/events/{{aiws.response.body.content[0].id}}/eligibility
Authorization: Bearer {{arun.response.body.accessToken}}

### 422 not-eligible with the same reasons
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{arun.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": {{aiws.response.body.content[0].id}}}

### 403 Organizers can't register (STUDENT only)
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": {{aiws.response.body.content[0].id}}}

### --- 5. Optimistic locking and capacity ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 200 Read the event: note "version" and seatsTaken (1: Arun)
# @name current
GET {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}

### 200 Raise capacity to 2 with the version just read. A new seat goes to the waitlist first, in the same
### transaction (Priya's second registration, if it was waitlisted, becomes CONFIRMED).
PUT {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "HTTPDEMO1", "title": "HTTP demo event", "categoryId": 1, "venueId": 1, "capacity": 2,
 "startsAt": "2099-11-14T03:30:00Z", "endsAt": "2099-11-14T09:30:00Z",
 "registrationOpensAt": "2099-10-01T03:30:00Z", "registrationClosesAt": "2099-11-13T12:30:00Z",
 "version": {{current.response.body.version}}}

### 409 The same edit with the version read before: "changed by someone else ... Reload it and try again"
PUT {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "HTTPDEMO1", "title": "HTTP demo event", "categoryId": 1, "venueId": 1, "capacity": 3,
 "startsAt": "2099-11-14T03:30:00Z", "endsAt": "2099-11-14T09:30:00Z",
 "registrationOpensAt": "2099-10-01T03:30:00Z", "registrationClosesAt": "2099-11-13T12:30:00Z",
 "version": {{current.response.body.version}}}

### 422 Capacity 1 while 2 seats are taken (no version: the check still applies)
PUT {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "HTTPDEMO1", "title": "HTTP demo event", "categoryId": 1, "venueId": 1, "capacity": 1,
 "startsAt": "2099-11-14T03:30:00Z", "endsAt": "2099-11-14T09:30:00Z",
 "registrationOpensAt": "2099-10-01T03:30:00Z", "registrationClosesAt": "2099-11-13T12:30:00Z"}

### --- 6. Closing ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 200 Organizer closes registration early (the scheduler does it at registrationClosesAt)
POST {{gw}}/api/events/{{created.response.body.id}}/transitions
Authorization: Bearer {{organizer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"to": "REGISTRATION_CLOSED"}

### 409 registration-closed
POST {{gw}}/api/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{arun.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": {{created.response.body.id}}}
